# Line endings are not a style question here. This project compares output
# byte for byte — three engines against each other, two compilers against
# each other, and every `.expected` snapshot against what a program printed.
# A file that arrives as CRLF on one machine and LF on another is a test
# that fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the compiler, which is
# exactly what happened the first time the suite ran on Windows.
#
# So: every text file is LF in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except what is not text.
*.png binary
